#: 3208e031ea054df0907a3b947fe16d52 of
#: utils.training.base_trainer.BaseTrainer:8
msgid ""
"The constructor wires everything: it calls :meth:`build_components` to "
"let the subclass assemble the model/optimizer/data from ``rc`` + "
"``data_src``, reads :meth:`build_callbacks` for any extra callbacks, then"
" runs :meth:`build` to finalize device, loaders, early stopping, logging "
"and checkpointing."
msgstr ""
"The constructor wires everything: it calls :meth:`build_components` to "
"let the subclass assemble the model/optimizer/data from ``rc`` + "
"``data_src``, reads :meth:`build_callbacks` for any extra callbacks, then"
" runs :meth:`build` to finalize device, loaders, early stopping, logging "
"and checkpointing."

#: f3980fb0ef304d93a8b879d95c0f2b96 of
#: utils.training.base_trainer.BaseTrainer:14
msgid "Subclasses implement:"
msgstr "Subclasses implement:"

#: 076c88c25fa64ce6b9b24d509c024e42 of
#: utils.training.base_trainer.BaseTrainer:16
msgid ""
":meth:`build_components`: Return a :class:`RuntimeComponents` holding the"
" model, optimizer, loss, scheduler, and train/val/test data built from "
"``rc`` + ``data_src``. Scalar knobs are read from ``rc`` directly, never "
"stored on the components."
msgstr ""
":meth:`build_components`: Return a :class:`RuntimeComponents` holding the"
" model, optimizer, loss, scheduler, and train/val/test data built from "
"``rc`` + ``data_src``. Scalar knobs are read from ``rc`` directly, never "
"stored on the components."

#: 46a8295529a4470b8e355b4c02d0857d of
#: utils.training.base_trainer.BaseTrainer:20
msgid ":meth:`build_callbacks`: Return extra callbacks (default ``[]``)."
msgstr ":meth:`build_callbacks`: Return extra callbacks (default ``[]``)."

#: 08c8c50cf09140baabfdd0cc18e9038a of
#: utils.training.base_trainer.BaseTrainer:21
msgid ":meth:`forward_pass`: Model forward pass for one batch."
msgstr ":meth:`forward_pass`: Model forward pass for one batch."

#: 76cda8a4037d42c09760aad181f8182b of
#: utils.training.base_trainer.BaseTrainer:22
msgid ""
":meth:`_compute_loss`: Training loss (default ``self.loss(y_hat, "
"y_label)``); auxiliary terms added here are excluded from val/test loss, "
"which always goes through :meth:`_compute_eval_loss`."
msgstr ""
":meth:`_compute_loss`: Training loss (default ``self.loss(y_hat, "
"y_label)``); auxiliary terms added here are excluded from val/test loss, "
"which always goes through :meth:`_compute_eval_loss`."

